# Template for /etc/exports.d/piwii.exports on the Pi (piwii.exports next to
# this file is the live one for this setup). Copy it there, replace
# <server-host-ip> with the address of the one machine that runs the piwii web
# server, then run `sudo exportfs -ra`. Only files ending in .exports are
# read, so this template does nothing where it is.
#
# piwii: staging area where finished games land before the Pi syncs them onto
# the game drive. Only the server host may mount it. People add games through the piwii
# web server, never by mounting this directly.
# all_squash maps the client to admin (1000) so files stay owned by admin.
# crossmnt lets the server host see the status/ tmpfs mounted inside staging.
/srv/piwii/staging <server-host-ip>(rw,sync,no_subtree_check,all_squash,anonuid=1000,anongid=1000,crossmnt)
# status/ is a RAM-only tmpfs (see srv-piwii-staging-status.mount). tmpfs has
# no stable filesystem ID, so it needs an explicit fsid. Read-only: the
# web server only reads status.
/srv/piwii/staging/status <server-host-ip>(ro,sync,no_subtree_check,all_squash,anonuid=1000,anongid=1000,fsid=7701)
